# The transport feedback for the cases play/transport-feedback.play leaves out (docs/rules/combat-rules.md, transport
# feedback), one case after another on layouts/transport-cases.jsonc, 3 seconds apart (each transport runs on until its
# target is full or it is cancelled, so later windows of the WAV hold the earlier parties too): the hero ship (Hero, kmartok) speaks its eventTransport line at its order and a destroyer with none (Plain) is
# silent and reports no gap; transprt.wav plays at every party, the derelict (captured) and friendly (crew added) ones
# included; msboard.wav plays only at a fight with a live hostile target, which none of these is. The targets of the hero
# and no-hero cases are neutral ships, so no unit fires. Each dump shows the end state of its case.
# Run it with --layout layouts/transport-cases.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
wait 0.5
select Hero
transport HeroPrize
wait 3
dump hero
select Plain
transport PlainPrize
wait 3
dump plain
select DerelictBoarder
transport Wreck
wait 3
dump derelict
expect Wreck team = 1
expect Wreck crew > 0
select FriendBoarder
transport Ally
wait 3
dump friendly
expect Ally crew > 4
